  "design_section": "7.18",
  "design_notes": [
    "The \"Fact\" column is stored in twin.",
    "\"Δv cost\" is a relative modifier on delta_v_m_s, copied as printed (−15% is −0.15; Expendable is 0). The design does not say whether the percentage is of the whole vehicle or of the first stage; scope vehicle is the reading used here.",
    "\"Cost effect\" is a refund fraction that applies only if the booster is recovered in flight (condition recovered). It is scoped to the first stage; the design does not name the cost it is a fraction of.",
    "\"(campaign: refurbish)\" on the parachute option has no number: it is the note of the refund modifier and a flag. \"(boostback + landing reserve)\" is the note of the RTLS Δv modifier.",
    "\"Ship cost $1 M\" (drone ship) is stored as cost_M 1.",
    "\"Needs grid fins & legs\" (RTLS): grid fins are a requires_part rule; no part in the catalog offers landing legs, so legs are a flag. Section 7.15 says grid fins are \"required for propulsive booster return\", so the drone-ship option carries the same requires_part rule although its own row does not repeat it.",
    "MG-24 Hoverslam is enabled by the two propulsive options (sentence under the table). The second half of that sentence is the category intro.",
    "Parachute + splashdown carries parachute_failure with the drop test as mitigation (8.4: \"No drop test\"; the drop test of 6.6 applies to parachutes).",
    "\"Weather-dependent\" (drone ship) is a flag: Weather Front in 6.8 is weighted by coastal launch sites, not by this option.",
    "No option is restricted to a contract. C8 requires the booster to land; that belongs to the contract requirements. Expendable has no model path: it adds no hardware."
  ],
